Provenance of the Nintendo 64 machine layer (runtime/guests/n64)

The register rules and timing below are ported from ares,
https://github.com/ares-emulator/ares, commit
0b928930af4cc59ed99e942996f0d3c815379388, ISC license (text below). The
code here is new C11 in relift's scheduler shape (closed forms and
scheduler events instead of per-cycle threads); each ported file keeps the
ISC notice in its header.

pi.c      the PI registers, the DMA's block shape, its duration from the
          domain timing, the busy and error rules
                                   n64/pi/io.cpp, dma.cpp, bus.hpp
vi.c      the VI registers, the line counter, field and leap pattern, the
          interrupt line rules, the frame edge
                                   n64/vi/vi.cpp, io.cpp

machine.c (MI, RI, SP, DP, AI, SI, PIF RAM, the boot words) and code.c are
relift's own, written from the public n64brew documentation.

